## Original Content
Anthropic is poised to debut on the stock market at a time when the public is increasingly upset about data centers and is fearful about AI taking jobs.

## Summary
Anthropic is preparing an IPO filing that will reportedly list public backlash against AI as a risk factor. The company is set to debut on the stock market amid rising public anger over data centers and widespread fears that AI will take away jobs.

## Key Points
- Anthropic's IPO filing will disclose AI-related public backlash as a risk factor
- Public sentiment is increasingly negative toward data centers
- Fears about AI-driven job displacement are growing among the public
- Anthropic plans its stock market debut despite this challenging public opinion environment


